1229		The distribution $D_{\mathrm{ALine}}$ is a uniform mixture of the
1230		distributions $D_{\mathrm{ALine},i}$ for $i \in \{1, \dots, m\}$, and
1231		likewise $D_{\mathrm{DLine}}$ is a uniform mixture of the
1232		$D_{\mathrm{DLine},i}$. As a consequence:
1233		\begin{enumerate}
1234			\item any approximation that holds on average over the line-point
1235			distribution $D_{\mathrm{Line}}$ with error $\delta$ holds over each
1236			restricted distribution $D_{\mathrm{ALine},i}$ and
1237			$D_{\mathrm{DLine},i}$ with error $2m\delta$;
1238			\item any approximation that holds on average over
1239			$D_{\mathrm{Line}} \times D_{\mathrm{Line}}$ holds over any product
1240			of restricted distributions with error $4m^2\delta$;
1241			\item in particular, by Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-xz-lines}, for any types
1242			$\mathrm{v}_1, \mathrm{v}_2 \in \{\mathrm{ALine},
1243			\mathrm{DLine}\}$ and any $i, j \in \{1, \dots, m\}$,
1244			\begin{equation}
1245				\label{eq:qld-xz-lines-restricted}
1246				\E_{(\ell_X,x) \sim D_{\mathrm{v}_1,i}}\
1247				\E_{(\ell_Z,z) \sim D_{\mathrm{v}_2,j}}
1248				\sum_{f_X,f_Z}
1249				\bra{\hat\psi}
1250				\big(T^{\ell_X,\ell_Z}_{f_X,f_Z}\big)_{\mathsf{A}\mathsf{A}'}
1251				\ot
1252				\big(\Id - \hat{Q}^{x,z}_{f_X(x),f_Z(z)}
1253				\big)_{\mathsf{B}\mathsf{A}''}
1254				\ket{\hat\psi}
1255				= O(m^2 \delta_P)\,.
1256			\end{equation}
1257		\end{enumerate}
1258	\end{lemma}
1259	\begin{proof}
1260		\uses{lem:qld-xz-lines, def:line-point-dist, def:consistency}
1261		The line-point distribution places weight $\tfrac{1}{2}$ on each of the
1262		axis-parallel and diagonal components and, within each component, uniform
1263		weight on the index $i$, so each restricted distribution carries mixture
1264		weight $\tfrac{1}{2m}$ in $D_{\mathrm{Line}}$. A nonnegative average that
1265		is at most $\delta$ therefore bounds each mixture component by
1266		$2m\delta$, and products of two such mixtures give the factor
1267		$(2m)^2 = 4m^2$. The instance \eqref{eq:qld-xz-lines-restricted} is item
1268		2 applied to the conclusion of Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-xz-lines}, whose
1269		$\simeq_{\delta_P}$ relation over two independent copies of the
1270		line-point distribution is precisely the statement that the left-hand
1271		side of \eqref{eq:qld-xz-lines-restricted}, averaged over
1272		$D_{\mathrm{Line}} \times D_{\mathrm{Line}}$, is at most $\delta_P$.
1273	\end{proof}
